  "intro": "It's Thursday evening, and the friends want to go out: to the cinema, or to hear old songs at the Cairo Opera House? Today's grammar joins two sentences with أَنَّ (that): سَمِعْتُ أَنَّ الْفِيلْمَ جَمِيل (I heard that the film is good). The noun after أَنَّ ends in -a, and a pronoun can be attached to it: أَنَّهُ (that he), أَنَّهَا (that she). Don't mix it up with أَنْ (to), which comes before a verb.",
